/01-app/02-guides/preserving-ui-state.mdx - just needs to be published to the live site - which should happen rather soon\n\n# Improve docs about handling state during navigation with cacheComponents #88622\n\nClosed\n\ngmoniava started this conversation in Ideas\n\nImprove docs about handling state during navigation with cacheComponents #88622\n\nJan 16, 2026 · 2 comments · 2 replies\n\nDiscussion options\n\n## \n\ngmoniava Jan 16, 2026\n\n### Goals\n\n  1. Improve docs about handling state during navigation with `cacheComponents`\n\n### Background\n\nBased on the docs with `cacheComponents`, routes are hidden via React `<Activity>` (state preserved) or fully unmounted (state lost) based on heuristics:\n\n> \"Next.js uses heuristics to keep a few recently visited routes \"hidden\", while older routes are removed from the DOM to prevent excessive growth.\"\n\nBecause state may or may not survive navigation, app authors lack a clear mental model for building pages safely:\n\n  * Can route-level state be relied on at all?\n  * Should routes always be treated as disposable?\n  * How should developers choose between local state, URL state, or external stores?\n\n### Proposal\n\nIt would help if the docs clearly framed cached route state as a performance optimization (not a correctness guarantee) and provided guidance on patterns that are safe regardless of whether a route is hidden or unmounted.\nThanks!\n\n\n## Replies: 2 comments · 2 replies\n\n  * Oldest\n  * Newest\n  * Top\n\nComment options\n\n### \n\ngmoniava Feb 1, 2026\n\nI found a gh comment related to this.\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\n0 replies\n\nComment options\n\n### \n\nicyJoseph Mar 16, 2026\n\nThere's a guide on canary about this: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/docs/01-app/02-guides/preserving-ui-state.mdx - just needs to be published to the live site - which should happen rather soon\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\n2 replies\n\nComment option